    "body": "A. Duie Pyle has opened a 44-door less-than-truckload (LTL) service center in the Cincinnati area, expanding its direct freight network in southwest Ohio just two weeks after opening a nearly 79,000-square-foot warehouse in central Pennsylvania.\nThe two most recent openings follow other investments aimed at expanding Pyle’s transportation and distribution capabilities beyond its traditional Northeast stronghold.\nIn January, FreightWaves reported that Pyle had acquired a 43-acre site at the Port 460 Logistics Center in Suffolk, Virginia, near the Port of Virginia.\nPyle has also expanded into U.S.–Mexico cross-border freight transportation over the last year.\nThe West Chester, Pennsylvania-based carrier announced Tuesday that the new service center in Cincinnati will strengthen freight connections between the Midwest region and its established Northeast and Mid-Atlantic markets.\nThe 44-door service center in the Cincinnati market extends Pyle’s direct less-than-truckload network into Southwest Ohio. (Photo: A. Duie Pyle)\nThe Cincinnati facility is expected to create 21 jobs initially, with employment projected to reach approximately 36 by the end of 2026, according to the company.\n“Growing our network is about being where our customers need us and creating stronger connections between the markets they serve,” Frank Granieri, chief commercial officer at A. Duie Pyle, said in a news release.\nThe opening is part of a broader westward expansion strategy announced in 2025, when Pyle outlined plans to establish additional service centers in Ohio to improve transit times and reduce its reliance on partner carriers.\nIn March 2025, John Luciani, Pyle’s chief operating officer for LTL operations, told FreightWaves the company was pursuing new terminals in Columbus, Toledo and Cincinnati to expand its direct overnight service footprint.\nThe carrier had acquired a former Yellow Corp. terminal in Bowling Green, Ohio, to serve the Toledo market and leased a facility in Columbus as part of that expansion.\nThe Cincinnati opening advances that strategy by bringing more freight movements in southwest Ohio directly into Pyle’s network, potentially reducing intermediate transfers and improving service consistency.\nThe Cincinnati opening follows Pyle’s Oct. 6 announcement of a new 78,760-square-foot warehouse in Camp Hill, Pennsylvania.\nThe Camp Hill warehouse sits adjacent to the company’s existing LTL service center, creating an integrated logistics campus that combines freight transportation and inventory storage.\nThe Camp Hill facility provides access to several major freight corridors, including Interstates 81, 76 and 83 and U.S. Route 15.\nPyle said the location is particularly suited for customers in healthcare, medical supplies and manufacturing that require consistent inventory availability and just-in-time replenishment.\nFounded in 1924, A. Duie Pyle is a privately held, family-owned transportation and logistics company offering LTL trucking, dedicated transportation, warehousing and brokerage services.\nWhy it matters: A. Duie Pyle’s investments strengthen the company’s direct-service capabilities in Ohio while expanding its ability to combine transportation and warehousing across the Northeast and Mid-Atlantic.\nUpcoming FreightWaves Events\nCompliance\nBrokerage Compliance Symposium\nThe day before F3. Every compliance issue you face - fraud exposure, carrier liability, FMCSA rules, cargo theft, insurance gaps - navigated by attorneys and operators defining best practices in a changing industry.\nOctober 26, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nAwards\nF3 Awards Dinner\nThe night before F3. FreightTech100 companies honored. FreightTech 25 and Shipper of Choice winners revealed live. Cocktail reception into dinner and live music - 300 industry leaders in one purpose-built room.\nOctober 26, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nFreightTech\nF3: Future of Freight Festival\nIndustry-defining keynotes, rapid-fire technology demos, and industry leaders networking in experiences across Chattanooga - plus the inaugural F3 Awards Dinner featuring the FreightTech and Shipper of Choice reveals.\nOctober 27, 2026 – October 28, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nCompliance Brokerage Compliance Symposium Oct 26 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nThe day before F3. Every compliance issue you face - fraud exposure, carrier liability, FMCSA rules, cargo theft, insurance gaps - navigated by attorneys and operators defining best practices in a changing industry.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now\nAwards F3 Awards Dinner Oct 26 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nThe night before F3. FreightTech100 companies honored. FreightTech 25 and Shipper of Choice winners revealed live. Cocktail reception into dinner and live music - 300 industry leaders in one purpose-built room.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now\nFreightTech F3: Future of Freight Festival Oct 27 – Oct 28 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nIndustry-defining keynotes, rapid-fire technology demos, and industry leaders networking in experiences across Chattanooga - plus the inaugural F3 Awards Dinner featuring the FreightTech and Shipper of Choice reveals.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now",
